## Parent

- Controller: #108
- Benchmark: #107
- Checkout recovery: #109
- Blob recovery: #110
- PR: #103

## Finding

The reconstruction used a `curl | while` process topology that allowed the parent and descendant curl processes to persist after the executor reported interruption/completion. They were explicitly terminated. No pipeline processes remain active.

This was an orchestration/lifecycle failure, not a blob-integrity failure.

## Current state

- 50/290 blobs accepted and validated by exact size and Git blob SHA;
- 240 blobs pending;
- one `.part` file isolated and rejected;
- no partial content promoted;
- no executable checkout;
- no preflight or B00–B03 benchmark started;
- existing embedding process was not touched;
- CT305 and production untouched.

## Required fix

Make reconstruction interruption-safe:

- use an explicit process group/session per reconstruction attempt;
- avoid untracked `curl | while` pipelines;
- use a parent supervisor that owns and reaps all descendants;
- handle SIGINT/SIGTERM/timeout deterministically;
- terminate the process group before reporting completion/interruption;
- wait for all descendants and verify no owned process remains;
- preserve only validated blobs and isolated `.part` files;
- checkpoint after each validated blob;
- resume from 50/290 without refetching accepted blobs;
- keep unrelated embedding processes untouched.

## Acceptance

- controlled interruption leaves no owned descendant process;
- resume continues from the 51st pending blob;
- all accepted blobs pass size and Git-SHA validation;
- audit records process lifecycle and cleanup status;
- checkout validation can proceed to #108.

